 "parsed": {
  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "The stages run in a fixed order, so blocking every technique at any one stage stops the attack. A single control can never be enough: every stage that can be blocked has two techniques, and no control blocks both. Recon cannot be blocked at all, since internal_reconnaissance has no blocking control. Two controls are sufficient, for example credential_vaulting plus edr closes off creds, which every later stage depends on. Other valid pairs include dns_monitoring + proxy_tls_inspection, or patch_struts/waf + email_filtering/security_awareness."
 },
